{"name":"Lark Wing","hex":"#c4ced1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lark","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various small, singing passerine birds of the family Alaudidae.","Any of various similar-appearing birds, but usually ground-living, such as the meadowlark and titlark."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To catch larks (a type of bird)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lark"},{"term":"wing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An appendage of an animal's (bird, bat, insect) body that enables it to fly.","A fin at the side of a ray or similar fish."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To injure slightly (as with a gunshot), especially in the wing or arm.","To fly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wing"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lark","blocks":[{"text":"Larks are passerine birds of the family Alaudidae. Larks have a cosmopolitan distribution with the largest number of species occurring in Africa. Only a single species, the horned lark, occurs in North America, and only Horsfield's bush lark occurs in Australia. Habitats vary widely, but many species live in drier regions. When the word \"lark\" is used without specification, it often refers to the Eurasian skylark (Alauda arvensis)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Alauda_arvensis_Linnaeus_1758.jpg/330px-Alauda_arvensis_Linnaeus_1758.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lark","wikidata":"Q29858"},{"title":"Wing","blocks":[{"text":"A wing is a structure which produces both lift and drag while moving through air. Wings are defined by two shape characteristics, an airfoil section and a planform. Wing efficiency is expressed as lift-to-drag ratio, which compares the benefit of lift with the air resistance of a given wing shape, as it flies. Aerodynamics includes the study of wing performance in air."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Wing.two.arp.600pix.jpg/330px-Wing.two.arp.600pix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wing","wikidata":"Q161358"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Greater_Hoopoe_Lark_-_Kutch%2C_crop.jpg/500px-Greater_Hoopoe_Lark_-_Kutch%2C_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Greater_Hoopoe_Lark_-_Kutch%2C_crop.jpg/1280px-Greater_Hoopoe_Lark_-_Kutch%2C_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Greater_Hoopoe_Lark_-_Kutch%2C_crop.jpg/500px-Greater_Hoopoe_Lark_-_Kutch%2C_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGreater_Hoopoe_Lark_-_Kutch%2C_crop.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Gray%27s_lark_-4770_-_Flickr_-_Ragnhild_%26_Neil_Crawford.jpg/500px-Gray%27s_lark_-4770_-_Flickr_-_Ragnhild_%26_Neil_Crawford.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Gray%27s_lark_-4770_-_Flickr_-_Ragnhild_%26_Neil_Crawford.jpg/1280px-Gray%27s_lark_-4770_-_Flickr_-_Ragnhild_%26_Neil_Crawford.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Gray%27s_lark_-4770_-_Flickr_-_Ragnhild_%26_Neil_Crawford.jpg/500px-Gray%27s_lark_-4770_-_Flickr_-_Ragnhild_%26_Neil_Crawford.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGray's_lark_-4770_-_Flickr_-_Ragnhild_%26_Neil_Crawford.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Spike-heeled_la